  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Joshua",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "Israel defeats the Amorites and their allies, and the Lord casts stones from heaven upon them—The sun and moon stand still—Many kings and cities are destroyed—The Lord fought for Israel.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now it came to pass, when Adoni-zedek king of Jerusalem had heard how Joshua had taken Ai, and had utterly destroyed it; as he had done to Jericho and her king, so he had done to Ai and her king; and how the inhabitants of Gibeon had made peace with Israel, and were among them;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "HEB Lord of righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:1",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "That they feared greatly, because Gibeon was a great city, as one of the royal cities, and because it was greater than Ai, and all the men thereof were mighty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Josh. 9:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 105
          },
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 151
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Josh. 9:3.",
            "prettyString": "Joshua 9:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "joshua",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:2",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore Adoni-zedek king of Jerusalem sent unto Hoham king of Hebron, and unto Piram king of Jarmuth, and unto Japhia king of Lachish, and unto Debir king of Eglon, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:3",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Come up unto me, and help me, that we may smite Gibeon: for it hath made peace with Joshua and with the children of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:4",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore the five kings of the Amorites, the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, the king of Eglon, gathered themselves together, and went up, they and all their hosts, and encamped before Gibeon, and made war against it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:5",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And the men of Gibeon sent unto Joshua to the camp to Gilgal, saying, Slack not thy hand from thy servants; come up to us quickly, and save us, and help us: for all the kings of the Amorites that dwell in the mountains are gathered together against us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:6",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "So Joshua ascended from Gilgal, he, and all the people of war with him, and all the mighty men of valour.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:7",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Lord said unto Joshua, Fear them not: for I have delivered them into thine hand; there shall not a man of them stand before thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Josh. 10:42; 21:44; D&C 98:37."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Josh. 10:42; 21:44; D&C 98:37.",
            "prettyString": "Joshua 10:42; 21:44; D&C 98:37",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "joshua",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 10,
                    "end": 10,
