                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:8",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Joshua therefore came unto them suddenly, and went up from Gilgal all night.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:9",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Lord discomfited them before Israel, and slew them with a great slaughter at Gibeon, and chased them along the way that goeth up to Beth-horon, and smote them to Azekah, and unto Makkedah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "OR put them to flight."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Isa. 28:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Isa. 28:21.",
            "prettyString": "Isaiah 28:21",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "isaiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 28,
                    "end": 28,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 21,
                        "end": 21
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:10",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, as they fled from before Israel, and were in the going down to Beth-horon, that the Lord cast down great stones from heaven upon them unto Azekah, and they died: they were more which died with hailstones than they whom the children of Israel slew with the sword.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 132,
            "text": "Ex. 9:18 (13–35); Ezek. 38:22; Rev. 16:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 57
          },
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 192
          },
          {
            "start": 230,
            "end": 234
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:11",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Then spake Joshua to the Lord in the day when the Lord delivered up the Amorites before the children of Israel, and he said in the sight of Israel, Sun, stand thou still upon Gibeon; and thou, Moon, in the valley of Ajalon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 148,
            "end": 151,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 20:11 (8–11); Isa. 38:8 (7–8); Hab. 3:11; Hel. 12:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:12",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sun stood still, and the moon stayed, until the people had avenged themselves upon their enemies. Is not this written in the book of Jasher? So the sun stood still in the midst of heaven, and hasted not to go down about a whole day.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "3 Ne. 1:15 (13–16). TG Astronomy."
          },
          {
            "start": 141,
            "end": 147,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Lost."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 108
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Scriptures, Lost.",
            "prettyString": "TG Scriptures, Lost",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Scriptures, Lost",
                "entryId": "tg-scriptures-lost",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:13",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And there was no day like that before it or after it, that the Lord hearkened unto the voice of a man: for the Lord fought for Israel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "Deut. 1:30 (29–30); D&C 105:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:14",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, unto the camp to Gilgal.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:15",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "But these five kings fled, and hid themselves in a cave at Makkedah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:16",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it was told Joshua, saying, The five kings are found hid in a cave at Makkedah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:17",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joshua said, Roll great stones upon the mouth of the cave, and set men by it for to keep them:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:18",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And stay ye not, but pursue after your enemies, and smite the hindmost of them; suffer them not to enter into their cities: for the Lord your God hath delivered them into your hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:19",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when Joshua and the children of Israel had made an end of slaying them with a very great slaughter, till they were consumed, that the rest which remained of them entered into fenced cities.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 160,
            "end": 165
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:20",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the people returned to the camp to Joshua at Makkedah in peace: none moved his tongue against any of the children of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:21",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Joshua, Open the mouth of the cave, and bring out those five kings unto me out of the cave.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:22",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And they did so, and brought forth those five kings unto him out of the cave, the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, and the king of Eglon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Josh. 12:10 (10–12)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 163,
            "end": 166
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:23",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when they brought out those kings unto Joshua, that Joshua called for all the men of Israel, and said unto the captains of the men of war which went with him, Come near, put your feet upon the necks of these kings. And they came near, and put their feet upon the necks of them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 260,
            "end": 263,
            "text": "This symbolized triumph of one people over another."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:24",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joshua said unto them, Fear not, nor be dismayed, be strong and of good courage: for thus shall the Lord do to all your enemies against whom ye fight.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:25",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And afterward Joshua smote them, and slew them, and hanged them on five trees: and they were hanging upon the trees until the evening.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:26",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass at the time of the going down of the sun, that Joshua commanded, and they took them down off the trees, and cast them into the cave wherein they had been hid, and laid great stones in the cave’s mouth, which remain until this very day.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 66
          },
          {
            "start": 222,
            "end": 234
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 10:27",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And that day Joshua took Makkedah, and smote it with the edge of the sword, and the king thereof he utterly destroyed, them, and all the souls that were therein; he let none remain: and he did to the king of Makkedah as he did unto the king of Jericho.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Josh. 12:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 148,
            "end": 152
          }
